  "vector_memory": {
    "semantic_summary": "ColliderBehaviour defines the physical geometry and interaction properties for an entity within a physics simulation. It inherits from EntityBehaviour and manages parameters like friction, restitution, and mass, utilizing a ColliderShape for geometric definition. The class registers itself with a PhysicsWorld upon initialization and ensures proper cleanup during destruction. It supports optional linking to a RigidBodyBehaviour for dynamic simulation participation."
  },
